window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Bonding a dragon brings the potential to save or destroy. The Dragon Dawn series continues.</b><br> <br> Now that he’s bonded the dragon Sashaak, Laric Mason must come to understand the power of the bond—and the potential power it grants him. Without a mentor, Laric struggles to understand the lessons of a dragon.<br> <br> Having imprisoned Talia, Laric and his friends know it's only a matter of time before mages come looking for her and Daelon.<br> <br> When Talia escapes, there's a new urgency. They must defend the village against a mage, but she's not after the village. She's after the dragon.<br> <br> Having seen the real Korthal, Laric knows he must protect Sashaak, because it's not only his village at stake.<br> <br> They might be all standing between Talia's ambitions. If she succeeds in forcing dragons to serve, other places will suffer a worse fate than what happened in his village.<br> <br> <b><i>Dragon Dawn</i></b><b> continues with another exciting dragon rider fantasy series by bestsellers D. K. Holmberg and Dan Michaelson.</b></p>"; 
